The chance is one in ten before your first gift so it's possible you
just are not patient enough.  But reading below I see a different
reason.

If it was randomly generated you should get a different artifact as your
first gift.  It has to be coaligned and racial so a chaotic elven
non-wizard can end up locked out by naming Sting and Orcrist in a game
that gave Stormy in a bones file.  The way to exit this lock-out is to
allow yourself to be crowned.  It counts as a first gift.  Being a class
with a specific guaranteed forst gift I do not think this lock-out can
happen.

> Yeah, I'm only killing hostiles, but I've not received any gifts at
> all from sacrificing.  Just four leaf clovers and golden glows.  I
> guess that means I just need to keep sacrificing and hope the RNG
> takes a break at some point.

Golden glows?  That's your problem!  Golden glows only happen when you
pray.  Artifact gifts only happen when you don't pray.  You have spent
an unknown number of your 30ish sacrifices bringing your prayer timeout
back down to zero and on praying.  If you want Magicbane do not pray at
all until you have it and are reconciled again after you get it.

